   "body": "### Description\n\nAfter upgrading from FastAPI 0.164.0 to 0.165.0, routes from routers added via `include_router` return 404. Only the first few included routers resolve correctly; the rest appear as `_IncludedRouter` objects in `app.routes` but their endpoints are unreachable. The OpenAPI spec at `/openapi.json` also omits the affected routes.\n\nDowngrading to FastAPI 0.164.0 restores normal behavior.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```python\n# repro.py \u2014 save and run with: pip install 'fastapi==0.165.0' uvicorn && uvicorn repro:app\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, APIRouter\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\nfor name in [\"alpha\", \"bravo\", \"charlie\", \"delta\", \"echo\", \"foxtrot\"]:\n    router = APIRouter()\n\n    @router.get(f\"/{name}\", endpoint=f\"get_{name}\")\n    async def endpoint(n=name):\n        return {\"router\": n}\n\n    app.include_router(router, prefix=\"/api\")\n\n\n@app.on_event(\"startup\")\nasync def show_routes():\n    for r in app.routes:\n        print(f\"{type(r).__name__:20s} path={getattr(r, 'path', '?')}\")\n```\n\n**Steps:**\n\n1. `pip install 'fastapi==0.165.0' uvicorn`\n2. `uvicorn repro:app`\n3. Try each endpoint: `curl localhost:8000/api/alpha` through `curl localhost:8000/api/foxtrot`\n\n**Expected:** All six endpoints return `{\"router\": \"<name>\"}`.\n\n**Actual:** The first few routers work; the remaining return `{\"detail\": \"Not Found\"}`. The startup log shows `_IncludedRouter` entries with `path=?` for the broken routers. `/openapi.json` lists only the working routes.\n\n### Environment\n\n- FastAPI 0.165.0 (Starlette 1.10.0)\n- Python 3.12 (`python:3.12-slim` Docker image)\n- Uvicorn 0.54.0\n- OS: Linux (Debian bookworm)\n\n### Workaround\n\nPin `fastapi<0.165` (i.e. 0.164.0 with Starlette <1.10.0).\n\n### Notes\n\nThis appears related to the introduction of `_IncludedRouter` in Starlette 1.10.0, which changed how `include_router` registers routes. The issue does not occur with Starlette <1.10.0 where routes are flattened directly into `app.routes`.",
