   "body": "### Description\n\nThis PR updates two outdated Pydantic v1 validation error JSON responses in `docs/en/docs/tutorial/handling-errors.md` to match the current Pydantic v2 format and runtime behavior:\n\n1. **Section *Override request validation exceptions*:**\n   - Updated default JSON response for `GET /items/foo` to use `\"type\": \"int_parsing\"`, the v2 error message, and the `\"input\": \"foo\"` field.\n   - Eliminates the contradiction with the plain-text example shown immediately below it.\n2. **Section *Use the RequestValidationError body*:**\n   - Updated JSON payload to include `\"type\": \"int_parsing\"`, v2 error message, and `\"input\": \"XL\"`.\n   - Adjusted `hl_lines=\"13-16\"` so highlighting remains on the `body` field after adding `input`.\n3. **Test coverage (`test_tutorial004.py`):**\n   - Tightened `test_get_validation_error` to assert the full formatted error string, ensuring the documented plain-text output is strictly verified in CI.",
